[2026-04-29 20:27:06] local.INFO: Executing tool: generate_powerpoint_presentation with args: {"title":"Weekly Meal Plan","content":"# Weekly Meal Plan Presentation\n\nThis PowerPoint will outline the 7-day meal plan in a clear, visual format. Each slide focuses on one day for easy reference, with bullet points for meals and simple icons or images implied (e.g., food visuals). Design style: mixed for a balanced, engaging look.\n\n## Slide 1: Title Slide\n- **Weekly Meal Plan Overview**\n- Balanced 7-Day Plan (~2,000 calories\/day)\n- Focus: Nutritious, easy meals with proteins, veggies, grains, and fruits\n- Prep Tips: Shop mid-week; batch cook grains\n- Presented by Kwati AI\n\n## Slide 2: Monday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Greek Yogurt Parfait** (400 cal)\n  - Greek yogurt, berries, granola, honey\n- **Lunch: Quinoa Salad** (500 cal)\n  - Chickpeas, cucumber, tomatoes, feta, lemon tahini dressing\n- **Dinner: Grilled Chicken** (600 cal)\n  - Chicken breast, steamed broccoli, brown rice\n- **Snacks:** Apple with almond butter; carrot sticks (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 3: Tuesday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Oatmeal Bowl** (400 cal)\n  - Oats, banana, walnuts, cinnamon\n- **Lunch: Turkey Wrap** (500 cal)\n  - Whole grain tortilla, turkey, spinach, avocado, hummus\n- **Dinner: Baked Salmon** (600 cal)\n  - Salmon, asparagus, sweet potato mash\n- **Snacks:** Mixed nuts; Greek yogurt (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 4: Wednesday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Green Smoothie** (400 cal)\n  - Spinach, banana, protein powder, almond milk\n- **Lunch: Lentil Soup** (500 cal)\n  - Lentils, whole grain bread, side salad\n- **Dinner: Tofu Stir-Fry** (600 cal)\n  - Tofu, bell peppers, zucchini, quinoa\n- **Snacks:** Pear; cheese stick (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 5: Thursday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Avocado Toast** (400 cal)\n  - Whole grain toast, avocado, poached egg, cherry tomatoes\n- **Lunch: Tuna Salad** (500 cal)\n  - Canned tuna over mixed greens, olive oil vinaigrette\n- **Dinner: Beef Stir-Fry** (600 cal)\n  - Beef, broccoli, carrots, rice noodles\n- **Snacks:** Orange; trail mix (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 6: Friday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Chia Pudding** (400 cal)\n  - Chia seeds, mango, coconut flakes\n- **Lunch: Veggie Burger** (500 cal)\n  - On arugula bed, sweet potato fries\n- **Dinner: Pasta Primavera** (600 cal)\n  - Shrimp, peas, zucchini in light pesto\n- **Snacks:** Celery with peanut butter; berries (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 7: Saturday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Scrambled Eggs** (400 cal)\n  - Eggs with spinach, whole grain toast\n- **Lunch: Chickpea Curry** (500 cal)\n  - Chickpeas, naan bread, yogurt\n- **Dinner: Roasted Pork** (600 cal)\n  - Pork tenderloin, Brussels sprouts, couscous\n- **Snacks:** Banana; dark chocolate (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 8: Sunday Meals\n- **Breakfast: Cottage Cheese Bowl** (400 cal)\n  - Cottage cheese, pineapple, almonds\n- **Lunch: Egg Salad Sandwich** (500 cal)\n  - On whole grain bread, side salad\n- **Dinner: Tempeh Stir-Fry** (600 cal)\n  - Tempeh, vegetables, wild rice\n- **Snacks:** Grapes; rice cake with hummus (200 cal total)\n- Daily Total: ~1,700 cal\n\n## Slide 9: Summary and Tips\n- **Weekly Total:** ~14,000 calories\n- **Key Benefits:** Varied nutrients, adaptable for vegetarians (swap proteins)\n- **Hydration:** 8 glasses of water daily\n- **Customization:** Adjust portions; consult a doctor for specific needs\n- **Next Steps:** Track your energy levels and tweak as needed!","document_type":"general","design_style":"mixed"}  
