[2026-04-29 20:32:28] local.INFO: Executing tool: generate_powerpoint_presentation with args: {"title":"Business Proposal: NutriWeek Meal Planning Service","content":"Slide 1: Title Slide\\n\\nBusiness Proposal: Launching \\\"NutriWeek\\\" Meal Planning Service\\n\\nPrepared by Kwati AI\\n\\nDate: April 29, 2026\\n\\nTarget Audience: Health conscious individuals and families\\n\\n\\nSlide 2: Executive Summary\\n\\nOverview: NutriWeek offers customizable weekly meal plans (~2,000 cal\/day) focused on balanced nutrition, ease of prep, and variety.\\n\\nMission: Help busy people eat healthier without the hassle.\\n\\nKey Benefits: Saves time, reduces food waste, promotes wellness.\\n\\nProjected Revenue: $50K in first year via subscriptions ($20\/month per user).\\n\\nInvestment Needed: $100K for app development and marketing.\\n\\n\\nSlide 3: Market Analysis\\n\\nIndustry Trends: Growing demand for meal prep services (global market $15B by 2026, per recent reports).\\n\\nTarget Market: 25 45 year olds, urban professionals (50M potential users in US).\\n\\nCompetitors: HelloFresh, Blue Apron but we focus on digital plans only (lower cost).\\n\\nOpportunity: Post pandemic health focus; 70% seek easier meal solutions.\\n\\n\\nSlide 4: Problem Statement\\n\\nChallenges Faced by Customers:\\n\\n- Time constraints from work\/life balance.\\n\\n- Decision fatigue in grocery shopping and cooking.\\n\\n- Inconsistent nutrition leading to health issues.\\n\\nOur Insight: 60% of adults report meal planning as a major stressor (survey data).\\n\\n\\nSlide 5: Solution: NutriWeek Service\\n\\nCore Offering: Digital weekly meal plans (e.g., our sample 7 day plan with breakfast, lunch, dinner, snacks).\\n\\nFeatures: Customizable for dietary needs (vegan, low carb); shopping lists; recipe videos; app integration.\\n\\nPricing: $20\/month basic; $35 premium with coaching.\\n\\nDelivery: Email\/PDF or app notifications.\\n\\n\\nSlide 6: Sample Meal Plan Overview (Based on Our 7 Day Template)\\n\\nDay 1 3: Protein focused (chicken, salmon, tofu).\\n\\nDay 4 6: Variety with beef, shrimp, pork alternatives.\\n\\nDay 7: Veggie heavy reset.\\n\\nTotal: ~14,000 cal\/week, adaptable.\\n\\nVisual: Include icons for meals (e.g., plate graphics).\\n\\nBenefits: Balanced macros, whole foods emphasis.\\n\\n\\nSlide 7: Business Model\\n\\nRevenue Streams:\\n\\n- Subscriptions (80%);\\n\\n- Partnerships with grocery apps (15%);\\n\\n- Upsells like premium recipes (5%).\\n\\nOperations: Cloud based platform; small team (5 people initially).\\n\\nScalability: AI driven personalization for growth.\\n\\nBreak even: 4,000 subscribers in year 1.\\n\\n\\nSlide 8: Marketing and Sales Strategy\\n\\nDigital Marketing: Social media ads on Instagram\/TikTok targeting wellness influencers ($30K budget).\\n\\nPartnerships: Collaborate with fitness apps and nutritionists.\\n\\nLaunch Plan: Beta test with 500 users; full rollout Q3 2026.\\n\\nSales Funnel: Free trial plan to convert 30% to paid.\\n\\n\\nSlide 9: Financial Projections\\n\\nYear 1: Revenue $50K, Expenses $120K (net loss $70K).\\n\\nYear 2: Revenue $250K, Profit $100K.\\n\\nAssumptions: 20% monthly growth; 10% churn.\\n\\nFunding Use: 50% tech dev, 30% marketing, 20% operations.\\n\\nROI: 3x in 3 years.\\n\\n\\nSlide 10: Call to Action\\n\\nNext Steps: Schedule a meeting to discuss investment details.\\n\\nContact: Kwati AI Team\\n\\nQ&A\\n\\nThank you for your time! Let's make healthy eating accessible.","document_type":"business","design_style":"corporate"}  
