[2026-05-02 17:53:45] local.INFO: Executing tool: generate_powerpoint_presentation with args: {"title":"Business Proposal: Launching EcoTech Incubator","content":"# Executive Summary\n- Proposal for EcoTech Incubator: Sustainable tech startup support\n- Mission: Foster green innovation with mentorship, funding, resources\n- Funding seek: $2M seed for 20% equity\n- Projected ROI: 25% in 3 years\n- Launch: Q3 2026\n\n# Company Overview\n- EcoTech Incubator: Delaware LLC focused on green tech\n- Core values: Innovation, sustainability, inclusivity\n- Support: 20 startups\/year in renewables, waste reduction, carbon-neutral chains\n- Founders:\n  - Jane Doe, CEO: 10+ years VC, ex-Google sustainability\n  - John Smith, CTO: PhD environmental engineering, 2 green tech startups\n- Location: San Francisco HQ, global virtual support\n- USP: AI matchmaking for mentors\/startups (90% funding success)\n\n# Market Analysis\n- Green tech market: $12.5B in 2026 \u2192 $45B by 2030\n- Drivers: Regulations (EU Green Deal), consumer demand\n- Competitors: Y Combinator, Techstars (general); niche opportunity in eco-tech\n- Target: Early-stage founders 25-40, North America\/Europe; 70% underrepresented\n- SWOT:\n  - Strengths: Expert network, hybrid model\n  - Weaknesses: Brand building\n  - Opportunities: Corporate partnerships (e.g., Tesla)\n  - Threats: Economic volatility\n\n# Services and Business Model\n- 6-month program:\n  - Mentorship: Weekly industry sessions\n  - Funding: $50K grants + investor intros\n  - Resources: Co-working, legal\/financial support, labs\n- Revenue:\n  - Equity: 5-10% in startups\n  - Fees: $500\/application\n  - Sponsorships: $100K+ from corporates\n- Projections: Year 1 $750K revenue; scale to $5M by Year 3\n\n# Marketing and Sales Strategy\n- Digital: SEO site, LinkedIn, webinars ($150K budget Year 1)\n- Partnerships: Universities (e.g., Stanford), accelerators\n- Funnel: Webinars \u2192 Applications \u2192 Acceptance (500 apps\/year, 4% rate)\n- Metrics: 80% completion, 50% follow-on funding\n\n# Financial Projections\n- Startup costs: $2M (office $300K, marketing $200K, ops $1.5M)\n- Pro Forma:\n  - Year 1: Revenue $750K, Expenses $1.8M, Net -$1.05M\n  - Year 2: Revenue $2.5M, Expenses $2M, Net $500K\n  - Year 3: Revenue $5M, Expenses $3.5M, Net $1.5M\n- Break-even: End Year 2\n- Funding: $2M for 20% equity\n\n# Team and Operations\n- Core team: 5 staff (CEO, CTO, Program Manager, Marketing, Finance)\n- Advisory: Climate scientists, Sequoia VCs\n- Timeline:\n  - Q2 2026: Funding & incorporation\n  - Q3 2026: First cohort\n  - Ongoing: Quarterly CO2 impact reports\n\n# Risks and Mitigation\n- Risk: Low applications \u2192 Mitigation: Digital outreach\n- Risk: Downturn \u2192 Mitigation: Diversify with grants\n- Exit: Acquisition by VCs or IPO of portfolio companies\n\n# Conclusion\n- Lead green tech revolution: Strong returns + sustainability impact\n- Contact: Jane Doe, jane@ecotechinc.com\n- Partner with us for investment opportunities","document_type":"proposal","design_style":"corporate"}  
